Static file middleware is called early in the pipeline so that it can handle requests and short-circuit without going through the remaining components. The static file middleware provides no authorization checks. Any files served by static file middleware, including those under wwwroot, are publicly available. For an approach to secure static files, see Serve static files in ASP.NET Core apps.
