### NoStore and Location.None properties
The NoStore property overrides most of the other properties. When this property is set to true, the Cache-Control header is set to no-store. If the Location property is set to None:
- The Cache-Control header is set to no-store,no-cache.
- The Pragma header is set to no-cache.
If the NoStore property is set to false and the Location property is set to None, the Cache-Control and Pragma headers are set to no-cache.
The NoStore property is typically set to true for error pages. The following code produces response headers that instruct the client not to store the response.

