#### Producers#
Job producers add jobs to queues. Producers are typically application services (Nest providers). To add jobs to a queue, first inject the queue into the service:

CODE EXAMPLE
LANGUAGE: typescript

```
import { Injectable } from '@nestjs/common';
import { Queue } from 'bull';
import { InjectQueue } from '@nestjs/bull';

@Injectable()
export class AudioService {
  constructor(@InjectQueue('audio') private audioQueue: Queue) {}
}
```

Now, add a job by calling the queue's add() method, passing a user-defined data object. Job data must be serializable, because jobs are stored in Redis. The shape of the data is arbitrary; use it to represent the semantics of your job.

CODE EXAMPLE
LANGUAGE: typescript

```
const job = await this.audioQueue.add({
  foo: 'bar',
});
```

