  "error": "Bad Request",
  "message": [
    "email: Invalid email address",
    "password: Too small: expected string to have >=8 characters"
  ]
}
```

The schema option is supported by @Body(), @Query(), and @Param(), as well as by @MessageBody() in gateways and @Payload() in microservices. Pass it as the only argument to validate the whole object, or after a property name to validate a single value:

CODE EXAMPLE
LANGUAGE: typescript

```
@Post('invitations')
invite(@Body('email', { schema: z.email() }) email: string) {
  return this.usersService.invite(email);
}
```

