```

Then, you can use the typings generation feature (as shown in the GraphQL quick start chapter) to generate the corresponding TypeScript definitions:

CODE EXAMPLE
LANGUAGE: typescript

```
export interface Character {
  id: string;
  name: string;
}
```

Interfaces require an extra __resolveType field in the resolver map to determine which type the interface resolves to. Create a CharactersResolver class and define the __resolveType method, which returns the name of the concrete type:

CODE EXAMPLE
LANGUAGE: typescript

```
@Resolver('Character')
export class CharactersResolver {
  @ResolveField()
  __resolveType(value) {
    if ('age' in value) {
      return 'Person';
    }
    return null;
  }
}
```

